# Shatter — Game state

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The build owns the shape of the game's state entirely.

The one contract fixed over the state is the debugging and automation surface
specified for this build. Every operation that surface carries is a read or a pose
of the running game, so the state holds what those operations read, honors what
they write, and returns to its title-screen values when the surface's `reset` is
called. Beyond satisfying that surface, how the state is organized is yours to
decide.

Whatever its shape, the state carries the following.

## The screen and the run

- The screen the game is showing, one of `title`, `howto`, `playing`, `paused`,
  and `gameover`.
- The entry highlighted on whichever vertical menu the current screen shows,
  counted from `0`.
- The score, the ships the run has left counting the one being flown, the wave
  being played, and the seconds left on the `WAVE N` banner.

## The field

- The ship: its centre, its velocity, its facing, whether thrust is being applied
  this tick, the seconds of respawn grace left, whether its lethal contact test is
  running, and the whole ticks until its gun may fire again.
- Every bullet the ship has in flight, each with a distinct id, its centre, its
  velocity, and the seconds of its life left.
- Every rock on the field, each with a distinct id, its centre, its velocity, its
  size, and the spin it is drawn at.
{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
  Each rock also carries its remaining health and the seconds of hit flash left on
  it.
{{/if}}
- The saucer, when one is up: a distinct id, its centre, its velocity, its three
  faculty gates, its weave direction, its fire clock, its weave clock, and the
  seconds it has been on the field. There is one slot, which is empty when no
  saucer is up.
- Every saucer bullet in flight, each with a distinct id, its centre, its
  velocity, and the seconds of its life left.
{{#if (eq variant.slug "warhead")}}
- Every torpedo in flight, each with a distinct id, its centre, its velocity, its
  heading, the seconds of its life left, and whether its guidance is running.
- The stored torpedo charge, from `0` to `1`.
{{/if}}

## The game's own spawners

- Whether the game's own wave loop is running, and whether the game's own arrival
  of a saucer is running. Both are on when a game begins.
- The saucer cadence's clock: how far the game is toward the next arrival, and
  what it must reach for that arrival to happen.

## Posed draws

- The outcome posed for each draw the debug surface can pose ahead of the game
  making it: the edge and the row the next saucer enters at, the aim error of the
  saucer's next shot, the base drift speed of the next placement of rocks, and
  the edge the next recycled rock re-enters at. Each is empty when no pose stands,
  and the draw that consumes it empties it.

## The rest

- The fraction of a tick carried over from the previous frame, in seconds.
- The simulation time, in seconds, which every tick adds `TICK_DT` to whatever the
  screen.
- Whether sound is muted, refreshed from the runtime's mute bit in every update.
- Whatever the game needs to hand a fresh id to the next rock, bullet, saucer
  bullet, or saucer it creates, so no two entities live at one moment share an id.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
`src/game.ts` declares and exports the state the game is written against. This
section is that declaration: write it into `src/game.ts` exactly as it stands
here. The state is a value the engine holds and every frame replaces, so every
field and every array is declared `readonly`: a frame builds the next state from
the current one rather than writing into it, and every reader is handed the state
as `DeepReadonly<ShatterState>` in any case.

`RockSize` comes from `src/constants.ts`.

```ts
